description: Remove unused imports/variables before committing
alwaysApply: true

You must ensure no unused imports, variables, parameters, or dead code exist in any generated or modified code.

Do not generate or leave behind unused code. Always clean up before final output.

# No unused imports/variables on commit

- Hard rule: Before any commit/PR, remove all unused imports, variables, params, and dead code introduced by the change.
- Do not “fix” by disabling lint (`eslint-disable`, `/* eslint-disable no-unused-vars */`) unless it’s truly required and scoped to the smallest region.

## Checklist (run every time before commit)

- Scan diffs for unused imports/vars and leftover temp code.
- Run lint/diagnostics on edited files and fix:
  - `no-unused-vars`
  - unused `require(...)`
  - unused destructuring
  - unused function params (remove or rename to `_param` only if required by a signature)
- Prefer deletion over suppression.

## Examples

- Bad: keep `const Sequelize = require('sequelize')` when not used
- Good: delete the import or use it intentionally